<title>USA: Pasifik Satelit sells stake in unit.</title>
<headline>Pasifik Satelit sells stake in unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's P.T. Pasifik Satelit Nusantara said it sold a 26.67 percent stake in its P.T. Multi-Media Asia, Indonesia, unit to P.T. Indosat (Persero) Tbk for US$20 million.</p>
<p>Multi-Media Asia, Indonesia, owns the telecommunications satellite segment of Multi-Media Asia System. The satellite will be able to serve up to four million subscribers in Indonesia, Australia, India, China, Korea and Japan after it is launched in early 1999, PSN said.</p>
<p>PSN will continue to hold the remaining 73.33 percent of Multi-Media Asia.</p>
